<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marib</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mariaba, Ma'rib</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marib is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> on the edge of the Ramlat al-Sabatayn desert, capital of Marib <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a>. In antiquity it was the capital of the kingdom of Saba, sustained by the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib-dam">Marib Dam</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> trade, and it has major ruins including the Awwam and Bar'an temples. Oil was found nearby in 1984, and in the recent civil war the city became a key government stronghold.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marib.jpg" alt="Marib" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: بدرالدين الشهاري · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MaribCity001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
